  ["Anything under internal/ can be imported only by code rooted at internal's parent. The cousin's shop gets a compile error, and you keep the right to delete."] = "internal/ 下面的任何东西，只有以 internal 的父目录为根的代码能导入。表哥的店会得到编译错误，而你保住删除的权利。",
  ["Append a &str to the end of a mutable String. Which method?"] = "把 &str 追加到可变 String 末尾。哪个方法？",
  ["Apply the timer wrapper to fry without changing its body. Which character goes before timer?"] = "不改 fry 的主体而应用 timer 包装器。timer 前面放哪个字符？",
  ["Arc shares ownership across threads; Mutex guards changes; atomics count without a lock."] = "Arc 跨线程共享所有权；Mutex 守护修改；原子类型不加锁地计数。",
  ["Arc, Mutex and atomics"] = "Arc、Mutex 与原子类型",
  ["Arc::clone(&sold) bumps the count, never copies the data. Same as sold.clone(), but the full path shows it is cheap."] = "Arc::clone(&sold) 只增加计数，从不复制数据。和 sold.clone() 一样，但写全路径能看出它很便宜。",
  ["Arc<Mutex<Receiver<Job>>> is Send + Sync, so it can be moved into every worker. The rail is shared, the pull is exclusive."] = "Arc<Mutex<Receiver<Job>>> 是 Send + Sync，所以可以移进每个工人。轨是共享的，取单是独占的。",
  ["Arc<Mutex<T>> is the shared-and-mutable idiom. Arc shares, Mutex guards; neither alone is enough."] = "Arc<Mutex<T>> 是共享且可变的惯用写法。Arc 负责共享，Mutex 负责守护；单靠哪一个都不够。",
  ["Arc<T> counts references atomically, so clones may live on different threads. Rc is cheaper but not Send."] = "Arc<T> 原子地计数引用，所以克隆可以住在不同线程。Rc 更便宜但不是 Send。",
  ["Arrays, slices, append"] = "数组、slice、append",
